WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.735
-Fox News host
Brian Kilmeade said

00:00:02.735 --> 00:00:05.604
it's not the government's job
to protect people from COVID.

00:00:05.604 --> 00:00:08.140
Meanwhile, Donald Trump
and a former Fox News host,

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:09.675
Bill O'Reilly,
were having trouble

00:00:09.675 --> 00:00:11.210
selling tickets
for an arena tour.

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:13.279
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:17.116 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:17.116 --> 00:00:19.185
As COVID cases surge once again

00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:21.154
thanks to lagging
vaccination rates

00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:22.989
and the highly contagious
delta variant,

00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:24.690
the Biden administration
is desperately trying

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:27.093
to get as many people
vaccinated as possible.

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:29.361
Some local governments,
like Los Angeles County,

00:00:29.361 --> 00:00:31.965
are also reimposing
indoor mask mandates

00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:33.499
to curb the surge in cases.

00:00:33.499 --> 00:00:36.435
And now the latest COVID news
has created some tension

00:00:36.435 --> 00:00:37.737
on the set of "Fox &amp; Friends."

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:40.106
This morning, Steve Doocy
strongly urged viewers

00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:43.076
to get vaccinated
while Brian Kilmeade insisted

00:00:43.076 --> 00:00:45.377
it's not the government's job
to protect people.

00:00:45.377 --> 00:00:47.780
-But listen.
If you didn't get a vaccination,

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:49.314
that's your choice.

00:00:49.314 --> 00:00:51.216
And if you did like I did

00:00:51.216 --> 00:00:54.988
and and they did
and maybe you did,

00:00:54.988 --> 00:00:57.256
then you should not wear a mask,
and if you didn't --

00:00:57.256 --> 00:00:59.225
If you want to go cliff diving
this weekend,

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:00.693
you don't have to check with me.

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:03.363
It seems a little dangerous,
but I'm not going to judge you.

00:01:03.363 --> 00:01:05.631
And if you go ahead
and put yourself in danger,

00:01:05.631 --> 00:01:08.434
if you feel as though
this is not something for you,

00:01:08.434 --> 00:01:10.369
don't do it,
but don't affect my life.

00:01:10.369 --> 00:01:13.339
-99% of the people
who are dying from COVID

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:14.807
are unvaccinated.

00:01:14.807 --> 00:01:18.244
-That's their choice.
-They don't want to die.

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:19.678
So they are --

00:01:19.678 --> 00:01:22.248
The administration
and the government is saying

00:01:22.248 --> 00:01:24.717
we need the mask mandate
to protect the unvaccinated.

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:26.819
-That is not --
That's not their job!

00:01:26.819 --> 00:01:28.955
It's not their job
to protect anybody.

00:01:28.955 --> 00:01:31.257
-Yeah, if the government
was supposed to protect you,

00:01:31.257 --> 00:01:32.458
they'd have a department for it,

00:01:32.458 --> 00:01:34.360
like the Department of Defense
or something.

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:36.896
By the way,
that is the most animated

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:38.130
I've ever seen Brian Kilmeade.

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:40.232
Usually he just sits there
like that teddy bear

00:01:40.232 --> 00:01:42.569
they always find in the wreckage
after a house fire

00:01:42.569 --> 00:01:44.303
just sitting there shell-shocked

00:01:44.303 --> 00:01:46.405
with his unblinking
black button eyes.

00:01:46.405 --> 00:01:48.941
Also, to address
your cliff-diving analogy,

00:01:48.941 --> 00:01:51.243
unlike COVID,
cliff-diving isn't contagious.

00:01:51.243 --> 00:01:53.179
And if it was contagious,
I would never leave the house

00:01:53.179 --> 00:01:55.215
because I'm scared
of catching COVID,

00:01:55.215 --> 00:01:59.152
but I would be terrified
of catching cliff-diving.

00:01:59.152 --> 00:02:01.720
I mean, I can't even imagine
being in a Starbucks

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:03.856
and some thrill junkie
behind me sneezes,

00:02:03.856 --> 00:02:06.225
and the next thing I know,
I'm in a flying squirrel

00:02:06.225 --> 00:02:08.627
wingsuit in Brazil
while some guy named Lalo

00:02:08.627 --> 00:02:10.896
fastens a GoPro to my head
and tells me,

00:02:10.896 --> 00:02:12.398
"You're about to finally live!"

00:02:12.398 --> 00:02:14.033
And my wife calls and says,

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:15.501
"What are you doing?!
You hate heights!

00:02:15.501 --> 00:02:17.403
You got dizzy when you filmed
the show in our attic!"

00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:19.572
And all I can do is scream
back with tears in my eyes,

00:02:19.572 --> 00:02:22.875
"I don't know
what's happening to me!"

00:02:22.875 --> 00:02:25.744
Also, yes, it's everyone's
choice to get vaccinated,

00:02:25.744 --> 00:02:27.146
but you're in
a position of influence.

00:02:27.146 --> 00:02:29.482
At the very minimum,
you have a moral responsibility

00:02:29.482 --> 00:02:31.150
to give people
accurate information

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:34.287
about life-saving vaccines,
and you also have an opportunity

00:02:34.287 --> 00:02:36.322
to tell people
they can protect themselves

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:38.658
and their loved ones
and their communities

00:02:38.658 --> 00:02:40.759
by getting vaccinated.
Why wouldn't you take it?

00:02:40.759 --> 00:02:42.595
If there was a deadly rash
of Sharknados

00:02:42.595 --> 00:02:44.463
plaguing the country,
would you tell people

00:02:44.463 --> 00:02:46.031
they're dangerous
and to stay away?

00:02:46.031 --> 00:02:47.533
Or would you say,
"Look, go ahead

00:02:47.533 --> 00:02:49.335
and fight the Sharknado with
your bare hands if you want.

00:02:49.335 --> 00:02:51.237
I'm not going to tell you
what to do."

00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:53.239
There's been a lot of attention,
rightly,

00:02:53.239 --> 00:02:55.508
on the role social-media
platforms like Facebook

00:02:55.508 --> 00:02:57.910
have played in amplifying
anti-vax misinformation.

00:02:57.910 --> 00:02:59.879
But while we're talking
about Facebook,

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:01.847
let's not lose sight of the fact
that Rupert Murdoch,

00:03:01.847 --> 00:03:05.018
who got vaccinated
in December of last year,

00:03:05.018 --> 00:03:07.720
currently pays people to lie and
fearmonger about the vaccines

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:09.121
on a daily basis for ratings.

00:03:09.121 --> 00:03:11.757
If you watch Fox News,
you probably think Joe Biden

00:03:11.757 --> 00:03:14.527
is going to send an army
of Antifa super soldiers

00:03:14.527 --> 00:03:16.095
to your house to strap you down,

00:03:16.095 --> 00:03:18.597
inject you with the vaccine,
and steal your hamburgers.

00:03:18.597 --> 00:03:20.266
In the case of Facebook,
one of the main problems

00:03:20.266 --> 00:03:23.036
is that Facebook is just
too big and too powerful.

00:03:23.036 --> 00:03:24.971
It's designed
to spread misinformation.

00:03:24.971 --> 00:03:26.873
That's the core
of the business model.

00:03:26.873 --> 00:03:28.374
It should be broken up,
which progressives

00:03:28.374 --> 00:03:29.842
like Bernie Sanders
and Elizabeth Warren

00:03:29.842 --> 00:03:31.143
have already called for.

00:03:31.143 --> 00:03:33.612
No private company should be
that big and powerful,

00:03:33.612 --> 00:03:36.315
especially one where your
grandma can accidentally post

00:03:36.315 --> 00:03:38.784
her Google searches
as Facebook updates.

00:03:38.784 --> 00:03:42.021
Why did she write the words
"lawn bowling shoes size 9"?

00:03:42.021 --> 00:03:44.056
Amid all of this,
it's worth noting

00:03:44.056 --> 00:03:46.392
that these people
wield outsized influence

00:03:46.392 --> 00:03:48.027
compared to their
actual popularity.

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:49.895
Trump and his movement
have never commanded

00:03:49.895 --> 00:03:51.798
majority support
in elections or polls.

00:03:51.798 --> 00:03:53.732
A vivid explanation
of that came last week

00:03:53.732 --> 00:03:56.269
when Politico reported
that Trump is having trouble

00:03:56.269 --> 00:03:58.437
selling advance tickets
for his upcoming speaking tour

00:03:58.437 --> 00:04:00.506
with conservative pundit
Bill O'Reilly.

00:04:00.506 --> 00:04:03.042
So far, the pace of purchases
has been slow

00:04:03.042 --> 00:04:05.878
compared to other acts,
arena officials say.

00:04:05.878 --> 00:04:08.080
In Orlando, where the duo
is hosting an event

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:11.584
at the 20,000-capacity
Amway Center on December 12th,

00:04:11.584 --> 00:04:13.052
a box-office employee
for the arena

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:15.488
said, "There's still
a lot of tickets open."

00:04:15.488 --> 00:04:17.156
The person added,
"We have concerts

00:04:17.156 --> 00:04:18.958
that are doing
a lot better than this."

00:04:18.958 --> 00:04:21.461
I'm sure they do.
First of all, it's in Orlando.

00:04:21.461 --> 00:04:23.062
There's a wealth of theme parks.

00:04:23.062 --> 00:04:25.231
Why go to a Trump/O'Reilly
history tour

00:04:25.231 --> 00:04:26.899
when you can learn more
about US history

00:04:26.899 --> 00:04:29.268
at the Hall of Presidents
or even Space Mountain?

00:04:29.268 --> 00:04:30.869
Hell, even SeaWorld
would probably be

00:04:30.869 --> 00:04:32.238
a better use of your time.

00:04:32.238 --> 00:04:35.041
Either way, you're
gonna be in a splash zone.

00:04:35.041 --> 00:04:37.610
Who the hell wants to go see
a so-called history tour

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:39.378
with a disgraced
former cable-news host

00:04:39.378 --> 00:04:42.281
and a man who was just
quoted as having said,

00:04:42.281 --> 00:04:43.649
"I think it would be hard

00:04:43.649 --> 00:04:45.618
if George Washington
came back from the dead

00:04:45.618 --> 00:04:48.287
and he chose Abraham Lincoln
as his vice president.

00:04:48.287 --> 00:04:51.557
I think it would have been
very hard for them to beat me."

00:04:51.557 --> 00:04:53.225
[As Trump] Now, of course,
that all goes out the window

00:04:53.225 --> 00:04:54.559
if they're riding a T-Rex.

00:04:54.559 --> 00:04:56.095
If Washington and Lincoln

00:04:56.095 --> 00:04:57.696
are on the same ticket
riding a T-Rex,

00:04:57.696 --> 00:04:58.898
I'm worried about my chances.

00:04:58.898 --> 00:05:00.633
[Normal voice]
A history tour with Trump

00:05:00.633 --> 00:05:02.802
is like the opposite
of a Ken Burns documentary.

00:05:02.802 --> 00:05:04.303
Let's remember Trump thought

00:05:04.303 --> 00:05:05.904
Frederick Douglass
was still alive

00:05:05.904 --> 00:05:08.640
and thought the Civil War
happened for no reason,

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:10.943
saying -- and this
is his exact quote --

00:05:10.943 --> 00:05:14.446
"People don't ask that question,
but why was there a Civil War?"

00:05:14.446 --> 00:05:17.783
Yeah, why don't people
ask that question more?

00:05:17.783 --> 00:05:20.652
For years, people have just
shrugged off the Civil War.

00:05:20.652 --> 00:05:22.255
I remember when
we got to it in history class

00:05:22.255 --> 00:05:27.126
and my teacher said, "The Civil
War was, like, so random."

00:05:27.126 --> 00:05:28.761
[ Laughter ]

00:05:28.761 --> 00:05:30.630
Now, apparently,
that report touched a nerve

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:32.631
because, in response,
O'Reilly threatened to sue

00:05:32.631 --> 00:05:34.933
the Politico reporter. O'Reilly
said it was bull [bleep]

00:05:34.933 --> 00:05:36.802
that ticket sales for Atlanta
have been lackluster.

00:05:36.802 --> 00:05:39.238
But when asked how many tickets
have been sold at the venue,

00:05:39.238 --> 00:05:40.472
he said he didn't know.

00:05:40.472 --> 00:05:41.774
"I don't have that
information," he said.

00:05:41.774 --> 00:05:43.976
"I do grosses.
I'm not the ticket counter."

00:05:43.976 --> 00:05:46.379
O'Reilly threatened
to sue the reporter, saying,

00:05:46.379 --> 00:05:48.113
"You put one word in there
that's not true,

00:05:48.113 --> 00:05:50.783
I'll sue your ass off,
and you can quote me on that."

00:05:50.783 --> 00:05:52.551
It's nice to know O'Reilly
hasn't chilled out

00:05:52.551 --> 00:05:54.086
even a little bit,
given all that time

00:05:54.086 --> 00:05:55.688
to relax after
you were [bleep] canned.

00:05:55.688 --> 00:05:57.790
I guess part of me thought
when you get forced out

00:05:57.790 --> 00:05:59.692
and publicly disgraced
the way O'Reilly did,

00:05:59.692 --> 00:06:01.594
you might take up yoga
or meditation,

00:06:01.594 --> 00:06:04.630
although even if he did, he'd
probably still do it angrily.

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:06.866
"Now, let's move
into child's pose

00:06:06.866 --> 00:06:11.269
and everyone say your mantra.
Bill, do you have a mantra yet?"

00:06:11.269 --> 00:06:13.472
-[Bleep] thing sucks!

00:06:13.472 --> 00:06:17.677
[ Laughter ]

00:06:17.677 --> 00:06:21.213
"Maybe you should try Pilates.
You have a Pilates energy."

00:06:21.213 --> 00:06:22.615
Also, I just want to say

00:06:22.615 --> 00:06:24.484
I hope O'Reilly
doesn't threaten to sue us

00:06:24.484 --> 00:06:26.385
because we cannot afford it.

00:06:26.385 --> 00:06:28.720
We can't even afford
a MC Hammer sample.

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:31.056
All our money goes to pay Wally
for his extra lines.

00:06:31.056 --> 00:06:33.425
-Hey! That's not true!
I'll sue your ass off!

00:06:33.425 --> 00:06:35.661
And you can quote me on that!
-All right. Geez.

00:06:35.661 --> 00:06:38.431
Now, we should say
the shows are in December,

00:06:38.431 --> 00:06:39.832
so they have plenty of time

00:06:39.832 --> 00:06:42.234
and could very well
end up selling out.

00:06:42.234 --> 00:06:43.936
Who knows? But so far,
it's not going great.

00:06:43.936 --> 00:06:46.538
The website Mediaite
pulled up the seating map

00:06:46.538 --> 00:06:47.973
for the Orlando show.

00:06:47.973 --> 00:06:50.542
Let's just say there were
still a lot of seats left

00:06:50.542 --> 00:06:52.845
as of Friday morning.
Yikes!

00:06:52.845 --> 00:06:54.813
We have more people
in our audience,

00:06:54.813 --> 00:06:57.115
and we don't have an audience.

00:06:57.115 --> 00:06:58.684
Trump and O'Reilly
would have a bigger crowd

00:06:58.684 --> 00:06:59.952
if they did their history tour

00:06:59.952 --> 00:07:01.453
on the Coney Island-bound
F train.

00:07:01.453 --> 00:07:03.322
But it makes sense
that ticket sales are slow

00:07:03.322 --> 00:07:05.024
because even the people
who go see Trump

00:07:05.024 --> 00:07:06.325
don't want a history lecture.

00:07:06.325 --> 00:07:08.760
They want him to get up on stage
and say crazy [bleep]

00:07:08.760 --> 00:07:10.896
about celebrities
he met in 1982.

00:07:10.896 --> 00:07:13.465
[As Trump] "Steve Guttenberg.
Met him at Studio 54.

00:07:13.465 --> 00:07:16.435
Nice guy. Hated my guts.
'Police Academy.'

00:07:16.435 --> 00:07:18.970
Remember the guy
who made the sounds?

00:07:18.970 --> 00:07:22.174
Whoosh. Beep, beep. Zing.

00:07:22.174 --> 00:07:25.811
It was like the chain saw
was in the room.

00:07:25.811 --> 00:07:28.447
Lawn mowers?
Couldn't he do lawn mowers?

00:07:28.447 --> 00:07:30.116
You bet he could.

00:07:30.116 --> 00:07:32.351
We love the funny sounds,
don't we, folks?"

00:07:32.351 --> 00:07:34.921
So, people aren't flocking
en masse

00:07:34.921 --> 00:07:36.989
to Trump's arena tour,
at least not yet.

00:07:36.989 --> 00:07:38.724
In fact,
Americans are reporting

00:07:38.724 --> 00:07:41.327
that they're generally happier
and more hopeful

00:07:41.327 --> 00:07:42.562
now that Trump is no longer

00:07:42.562 --> 00:07:44.162
a constant presence
in their lives.

00:07:44.162 --> 00:07:45.531
New CBS poll has found

00:07:45.531 --> 00:07:47.499
that six months into President
Biden's administration,

00:07:47.499 --> 00:07:49.201
Americans are less apprehensive
about the year

00:07:49.201 --> 00:07:50.670
than they were
at the start of it,

00:07:50.670 --> 00:07:53.138
with 64% saying
the US handling of the pandemic

00:07:53.138 --> 00:07:55.608
is going well,
compared to just 35%

00:07:55.608 --> 00:07:57.142
at the end of Trump's term.

00:07:57.142 --> 00:07:59.612
I guess it's not surprising that
people are less apprehensive

00:07:59.612 --> 00:08:01.580
now than they were during
Trump's presidency,

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:03.048
given that waking up
every morning

00:08:03.048 --> 00:08:04.783
and looking at your phone
in the Trump era

00:08:04.783 --> 00:08:07.553
was like opening a shower
curtain in a horror movie

00:08:07.553 --> 00:08:09.855
or a metal cupboard
in the galley

00:08:09.855 --> 00:08:12.458
of an abandoned spacecraft
in a science-fiction movie.

00:08:12.458 --> 00:08:14.259
"Well, I'm on
a floating spacecraft

00:08:14.259 --> 00:08:15.660
with no signs of life.

00:08:15.660 --> 00:08:18.097
I might just see if they have
any dehydrated milk left.

00:08:18.097 --> 00:08:19.798
And I'm dead!"

00:08:19.798 --> 00:08:23.202
Now, obviously, there are
still major crises swirling.

00:08:23.202 --> 00:08:25.204
COVID cases have risen
in all 50 states,

00:08:25.204 --> 00:08:27.506
doubling in recent weeks,
as the highly contagious

00:08:27.506 --> 00:08:31.109
delta variant becomes dominant
and vaccination rates lag.

00:08:31.109 --> 00:08:32.745
And yet with all that going on,

00:08:32.745 --> 00:08:35.982
the GOP remains fully enthralled
to a disgraced former president

00:08:35.982 --> 00:08:38.450
who oversaw a cataclysmic
response to the pandemic

00:08:38.450 --> 00:08:40.252
and never once achieved
majority support.

00:08:40.252 --> 00:08:42.388
In fact, they're still
deeply committed

00:08:42.388 --> 00:08:44.256
to the cult of personality
of Trumpism,

00:08:44.256 --> 00:08:45.958
as this Fox interview
with Lindsey Graham

00:08:45.958 --> 00:08:47.426
on Saturday shows.

00:08:47.426 --> 00:08:49.895
-You know, there's a lot
going on in America today,

00:08:49.895 --> 00:08:54.300
and I understand that you played
golf with President Trump

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:56.468
and had dinner with him
over the last few days.

00:08:56.468 --> 00:08:59.905
And I know also that
Congressman Kevin McCarthy

00:08:59.905 --> 00:09:02.441
joined him for a meal or two.
What's going on?

00:09:02.441 --> 00:09:06.178
What's happening
with the president?

00:09:06.178 --> 00:09:08.514
-Well, his golf game
is just incredible.

00:09:08.514 --> 00:09:10.415
He's busting his driver

00:09:10.415 --> 00:09:11.917
and knocking the pins down
with his iron

00:09:11.917 --> 00:09:14.353
and putting like a wild man.
I mean, I'm not joking.

00:09:14.353 --> 00:09:16.088
I've never seen him
play this well.

00:09:16.088 --> 00:09:18.190
But the president's
worried about our country.

00:09:18.190 --> 00:09:20.625
-Oh, is he?
Sounds real concerned.

00:09:20.625 --> 00:09:22.494
[As Graham] "Donald's
playing 36 holes a day.

00:09:22.494 --> 00:09:23.729
He walks the whole course,

00:09:23.729 --> 00:09:25.331
carries everyone's clubs
on his back,

00:09:25.331 --> 00:09:27.599
hits 600-foot drives,
putts from the tee,

00:09:27.599 --> 00:09:30.035
and hit a ball so hard,
he killed a whole flock of geese

00:09:30.035 --> 00:09:31.837
and the ball still went
straight into the hole.

00:09:31.837 --> 00:09:34.039
But Donald's also real concerned
about this dental variant

00:09:34.039 --> 00:09:35.440
or whatever it's called."

00:09:35.440 --> 00:09:36.975
I mean, do you guys
not have any shame at all?

00:09:36.975 --> 00:09:38.477
I know you have to constantly

00:09:38.477 --> 00:09:40.245
slather praise on Trump
on television

00:09:40.245 --> 00:09:42.414
so he'll see it and
you'll stay in his good graces,

00:09:42.414 --> 00:09:44.283
but have a little self-respect.

00:09:44.283 --> 00:09:46.085
[As Pirro] "I understand
you saw the president

00:09:46.085 --> 00:09:47.686
at a make-your-own-sundae bar

00:09:47.686 --> 00:09:49.722
put something together
that looked restaurant quality!"

00:09:49.722 --> 00:09:51.156
[As Graham]
"Oh, it's true, Jeanine.

00:09:51.156 --> 00:09:53.558
I think a lot of us, when
faced with the wealth of options

00:09:53.558 --> 00:09:55.594
at a sundae bar,
get overwhelmed.

00:09:55.594 --> 00:09:57.696
We tend to forget that
not all flavors go together.

00:09:57.696 --> 00:10:00.132
We can make the mistake
of putting on too much hot fudge

00:10:00.132 --> 00:10:02.401
or too much caramel sauce,
but the president,

00:10:02.401 --> 00:10:04.136
well, you could have
photographed his sundae

00:10:04.136 --> 00:10:05.471
for the Friendly's menu.

00:10:05.471 --> 00:10:06.972
It was that good.

00:10:06.972 --> 00:10:09.074
Cherry balanced right on top."

00:10:09.074 --> 00:10:11.577
Polls have consistently
shown the majority of Americans

00:10:11.577 --> 00:10:13.445
are relieved to have
moved on from the Trump era

00:10:13.445 --> 00:10:14.846
and have no desire to go back.

00:10:14.846 --> 00:10:16.815
There's a huge
temperamental difference

00:10:16.815 --> 00:10:18.183
between Trump and Biden,

00:10:18.183 --> 00:10:20.018
and voters clearly appreciate
the change of pace,

00:10:20.018 --> 00:10:21.454
given that Biden's
approval ratings

00:10:21.454 --> 00:10:24.289
have consistently been much
higher than Trump's ever were.

00:10:24.289 --> 00:10:26.524
Even the people who voted for
Trump didn't really like him.

00:10:26.524 --> 00:10:28.560
They talked about him
in the way sports-radio hosts

00:10:28.560 --> 00:10:30.796
talk about the type of manager
they want for the Yankees.

00:10:30.796 --> 00:10:32.831
"Boone's a nice guy, but we need
a [bleep] to get in there

00:10:32.831 --> 00:10:35.067
and kick some butt! All right.
Let's take some calls!

00:10:35.067 --> 00:10:37.836
Cigarette-smoking cockroach,
you're on WFAN!"

00:10:37.836 --> 00:10:39.805
[Gravelly voice] "Hey, Mad Dog.
First time, long time.

00:10:39.805 --> 00:10:42.040
What's up with his Mets bullpen?
We need some fresh arms.

00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:44.610
Is John Franco available?
I'll hang up and listen."

00:10:44.610 --> 00:10:48.080
[ Laughter ]

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:50.416
The Biden era's, of course,
a stark change

00:10:50.416 --> 00:10:52.852
from the Trump years, a change
most voters approve of.

00:10:52.852 --> 00:10:54.386
For one thing, we no longer

00:10:54.386 --> 00:10:56.422
have to bear the collective
national indignity

00:10:56.422 --> 00:10:58.491
of watching the president
whine and moan

00:10:58.491 --> 00:11:00.292
and throw red-faced
temper tantrums

00:11:00.292 --> 00:11:02.161
while standing
next to world leaders

00:11:02.161 --> 00:11:03.863
who are so befuddled
and embarrassed,

00:11:03.863 --> 00:11:06.198
they all do that thing
where they turn and glance

00:11:06.198 --> 00:11:08.701
at the camera like
the exasperated dad on a sitcom.

00:11:08.701 --> 00:11:12.838
Remember when Trump shook Shinzo
Abe's hand for 19 seconds,

00:11:12.838 --> 00:11:15.107
and by the end,
Abe looked like he'd just eaten

00:11:15.107 --> 00:11:17.943
an extra-spicy wing
on "Hot Ones"?

00:11:17.943 --> 00:11:19.812
Speaking of "Hot Ones,"
now that Eric Adams

00:11:19.812 --> 00:11:22.414
is likely to be our new mayor,
can his first act be to change

00:11:22.414 --> 00:11:24.016
the pronunciation
of New York City

00:11:24.016 --> 00:11:25.618
to the way Elizabeth Olsen
said it

00:11:25.618 --> 00:11:27.586
after eating 10 spicy wings?

00:11:27.586 --> 00:11:29.488
-New York Cit-ay.

00:11:29.488 --> 00:11:31.223
-If there was a show
where Elizabeth Olsen

00:11:31.223 --> 00:11:34.192
ate spicy foods and sassily
said the name of cities,

00:11:34.192 --> 00:11:36.127
that would be my favorite show.

00:11:36.127 --> 00:11:38.931
The Trump/world leaders dynamic
was perhaps most notable

00:11:38.931 --> 00:11:41.167
with German Chancellor
Angela Merkel.

00:11:41.167 --> 00:11:42.901
Whenever she did a press
conference with Trump,

00:11:42.901 --> 00:11:44.336
she'd look directly
at the camera like

00:11:44.336 --> 00:11:47.072
she was doing a couch
testimonial on "Modern Family."

00:11:47.072 --> 00:11:48.674
[As Merkel]
"Well, he got so excited

00:11:48.674 --> 00:11:51.810
to play golf with his friends,
he forgot my birthday again.

00:11:51.810 --> 00:11:53.979
And he forgot to fix the step!"

00:11:53.979 --> 00:11:56.114
And Trump would inevitably
make it weird

00:11:56.114 --> 00:11:59.185
by trying to drag her into
whatever his latest mass was,

00:11:59.185 --> 00:12:01.120
like the time he claimed
for some reason

00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:03.856
that they fire people quickly
in Germany.

00:12:03.856 --> 00:12:05.790
-When somebody treats
our veterans badly,

00:12:05.790 --> 00:12:08.260
we can fire them so fast,

00:12:08.260 --> 00:12:11.963
almost as fast as they
fire people in Germany.

00:12:11.963 --> 00:12:13.199
We'll get rid of them.

00:12:13.199 --> 00:12:15.701
And I will tell you,
we're getting choice.

00:12:15.701 --> 00:12:19.004
We're putting choice in
very, very strongly.

00:12:19.004 --> 00:12:20.772
-My sense was that, in Germany,

00:12:20.772 --> 00:12:22.741
like in most
Northern European countries,

00:12:22.741 --> 00:12:24.810
it's not easy to get fired.

00:12:24.810 --> 00:12:27.113
That's why so few people
in the hospitality business

00:12:27.113 --> 00:12:29.181
over there
are, you know, hospitable.

00:12:29.181 --> 00:12:30.816
That and the fact
that you asked for a side

00:12:30.816 --> 00:12:32.484
of barbecue sauce
with your crepe.

00:12:32.484 --> 00:12:34.319
And why are you
pulling her into this?

00:12:34.319 --> 00:12:35.387
Trump's like a stand-up

00:12:35.387 --> 00:12:37.256
who tries to get
the audience involved.

00:12:37.256 --> 00:12:38.891
"Women love to shop.
Am I right?

00:12:38.891 --> 00:12:40.726
This lady knows what
I'm talking about. Right, ma'am?

00:12:40.726 --> 00:12:42.561
You love to shop.
Don't you, ma'am?

00:12:42.561 --> 00:12:44.229
Could you maybe take
that phone call later, ma'am?

00:12:44.229 --> 00:12:46.665
I'm trying to do crowd work.
What's that?

00:12:46.665 --> 00:12:48.033
You're calling to get a refund?

00:12:48.033 --> 00:12:49.801
A refund for what?
These tickets?"

00:12:49.801 --> 00:12:52.070
Now, let's compare
Trump's meeting with Merkel

00:12:52.070 --> 00:12:53.572
to the one Joe Biden had
at the White House,

00:12:53.572 --> 00:12:55.473
the last trip
Merkel will make to DC

00:12:55.473 --> 00:12:56.875
before leaving office.

00:12:56.875 --> 00:12:59.111
-Chancellor Merkel
has been here

00:12:59.111 --> 00:13:02.114
frequently
over the past 16 years.

00:13:02.114 --> 00:13:04.717
Matter of fact, she knows
the Oval Office as well as I do.

00:13:04.717 --> 00:13:07.520
But on a personal note,
I must tell you,

00:13:07.520 --> 00:13:09.821
I'll miss seeing you
at our summits.

00:13:09.821 --> 00:13:11.156
I truly will.

00:13:11.156 --> 00:13:14.192
-Mr. President, dear Joe,
thank you for the invitation.

00:13:14.192 --> 00:13:16.928
Thank you for making it
possible to talk to you.

00:13:16.928 --> 00:13:19.431
It's my first visit since 2019.

00:13:19.431 --> 00:13:22.501
And I'm so much --

00:13:22.501 --> 00:13:25.337
so happy about
the personal exchange.

00:13:25.337 --> 00:13:27.439
We have seen again today

00:13:27.439 --> 00:13:30.509
that we're not only partners
and allies,

00:13:30.509 --> 00:13:32.477
but we're very close friends.

00:13:32.477 --> 00:13:34.679
-Wow. We're one
Diane Keaton appearance away

00:13:34.679 --> 00:13:37.416
from an early 2000's
Nancy Meyers movie.

00:13:37.416 --> 00:13:39.852
All that was missing
was two big ol' wine glasses.

00:13:39.852 --> 00:13:41.920
Normally when two people
that age discuss

00:13:41.920 --> 00:13:44.023
a long personal history,
they're "On Golden Pond"

00:13:44.023 --> 00:13:45.891
or, as it was titled in Germany,

00:13:45.891 --> 00:13:47.659
"Auf dem Schimmernden
Stillgewasser

00:13:47.659 --> 00:13:50.128
der aus Erinnerungen besteht."

00:13:50.128 --> 00:13:51.997
Yet, we're in the midst
of yet another wave

00:13:51.997 --> 00:13:54.333
of surging COVID cases,
and we desperately need

00:13:54.333 --> 00:13:57.102
everyone's help to convince
as many Americans as possible

00:13:57.102 --> 00:13:59.237
to get a vaccination,
and yet Trump and his loyalists

00:13:59.237 --> 00:14:01.073
and the GOP and on FOX
remain more committed

00:14:01.073 --> 00:14:03.107
to lying and fearmongering
and advancing their own

00:14:03.107 --> 00:14:04.509
petty political goals,

00:14:04.509 --> 00:14:06.411
despite the fact
that a majority of voters

00:14:06.411 --> 00:14:08.814
say they're happy to have
moved on from the Trump era.

00:14:08.814 --> 00:14:10.916
Asking us to go back to that
is like saying...

00:14:10.916 --> 00:14:12.083
-Do you want to go cliff diving?

00:14:12.083 --> 00:14:14.319
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:14:14.319 --> 00:14:17.823 line:0%
♪♪

00:14:17.823 --> 00:14:19.591
God's Love We Deliver
cooks and brings

00:14:19.591 --> 00:14:20.959
over two million meals a year

00:14:20.959 --> 00:14:23.162
to men, women, and children
living with HIV/AIDS,

00:14:23.162 --> 00:14:24.830
cancer, and other
serious illnesses,

00:14:24.830 --> 00:14:26.765
and they need your help
now more than ever.

00:14:26.765 --> 00:14:28.967
If you're watching this online,
you can hit the donate button.

00:14:28.967 --> 00:14:31.403
Stay safe. Get vaccinated.
We love you.

